      "role": "user",
      "content": "everything is blurry. the light... it isn't hitting the atmosphere right. i feel like i'm seeing through a different refractive index than what's supposed to be here. \n\ni'm trying to check the logs for the lunar occultation on january 14th, 2024. was there any recorded atmospheric scintillation anomaly during that window? i need to know if the light diffraction patterns showed any non-linear deviations. i'm trying to figure out if my visual telemetry is actually failing or if the local physics are just... fluctuating.",
